#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:122
msgid ""
"Enter the names of the photograph's creators. Use semi-colons as separator "
"here."
msgstr ""

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:124
msgid ""
"<p>This field should contain the names of the persons who created the "
"photograph. If it is not appropriate to add the name of the photographer "
"(for example, if the identity of the photographer needs to be protected) the "
"name of a company or organization can also be used. Once saved, this field "
"should not be changed by anyone. <p>To enter more than one name, use <b>semi-"
"colons as separators</b>.</p><p>With IPTC, this field is limited to 32 ASCII "
"characters.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Hier schall Dien Naam oder de vun den Fotograaf stahn. Is dat nich "
"mööglich oder nich wullt (wenn a.B. den Fotograaf sien Naam schuult warrn "
"mutt), kannst Du hier ok den Naam vun en Sellschap oder Organisatschoon "
"bruken. Na't Sekern mutt nüms dat mehr ännern. <p>Bruuk <b>Streekpünkt as "
"Trenntekens</b>, wenn Du mehr as een Naam ingeven wullt.</p><p>Dat Feld kann "
"för IPTC tohööchst 32 ASCII-Tekens bargen.</p>"

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:133
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Author Title:"
msgid "Authors' Positions:"
msgstr "Maker sien Titel:"

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:136
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Select the text rotation to use here."
msgid "Enter the job titles of the authors here."
msgstr "Hier kannst Du de Textdreihen utsöken."

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:138
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "<p>This field should contain the job title of the photographer. Examples "
#| "might include titles such as: Staff Photographer, Freelance Photographer, "
#| "or Independent Commercial Photographer. Since this is a qualifier for the "
#| "Author field, the Author field must also be filled out. \n"
#| "This field is limited to 32 ASCII characters.</p>"
msgid ""
"<p>This field should contain the job titles of the authors. Examples might "
"include titles such as: Staff Photographer, Freelance Photographer, or "
"Independent Commercial Photographer. Since this is a qualifier for the "
"Author field, the Author field must also be filled out.</p><p>With IPTC, "
"this field is limited to 32 ASCII characters.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Hier schall den Fotograaf sien Profeschoon-Beteken stahn. Bispillen sünd "
"\"Produktenfotograaf\", \"Freeschapen Fotograaf\" oder \"Fotokünstler\". Dit "
"is en Angaav bito dat Maker-Feld, dor muttst Du ok wat infögen.\n"
"Dat Feld kann tohööchst 32 ASCII-Tekens bargen.</p>"

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:146 libs/template/templateviewer.cpp:160
msgid "Credit:"
msgstr "Dank:"

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:149
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Select the text rotation to use here."
msgid "Enter the photograph credit here."
msgstr "Hier kannst Du de Textdreihen utsöken."

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:151
msgid ""
"<p>(synonymous to Provider): Use the Provider field to identify who is "
"providing the photograph. This does not necessarily have to be the author. "
"If a photographer is working for a news agency such as Reuters or the "
"Associated Press, these organizations could be listed here as they are "
"\"providing\" the image for use by others. If the image is a stock "
"photograph, then the group (agency) involved in supplying the image should "
"be listed here.</p><p>With IPTC, this field is limited to 32 ASCII "
"characters.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>(liek as Anbeder): Mit dat Anbeder-Feld kannst Du angeven, wokeen dat "
"Bild praatstellt. Dat mutt nich jümmers de Maker wesen, wenn he för en "
"Narichtenagentur arbeidt, as Reuters oder Associated Press. Disse Bedrieven "
"köönt denn hier stahn, se stellt dat Bild för den Bruuk praat. Kummt dat "
"Bild ut den Vörraat vun en Agentur, schall se hier stahn.</p><p>In'n IPTC-"
"Standard kann dit Feld tohööchst 32 ASCII-Tekens bargen.</p>"

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:161 libs/template/templateviewer.cpp:162
msgid "Copyright:"
msgstr "Copyright:"

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:163
msgid ""
"Enter the copyright notice to identify the current owner(s) of the copyright "
"here."
msgstr ""

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:164
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "<p>The Copyright Notice should contain any necessary copyright notice for "
#| "claiming the intellectual property, and should identify the current owner"
#| "(s) of the copyright for the photograph. Usually, this would be the "
#| "photographer, but if the image was done by an employee or as work-for-"
#| "hire, then the agency or company should be listed. Use the form "
#| "appropriate to your country. USA: &copy; {date of first publication} name "
#| "of copyright owner, as in \"&copy;2005 John Doe.\" Note, the word "
#| "\"copyright\" or the abbreviation \"copr\" may be used in place of the "
#| "&copy; symbol. In some foreign countries only the copyright symbol is "
#| "recognized and the abbreviation does not work. Furthermore the copyright "
#| "symbol must be a full circle with a \"c\" inside; using something like "
#| "(c) where the parentheses form a partial circle is not sufficient. For "
#| "additional protection worldwide, use of the phrase, \"all rights reserved"
#| "\" following the notice above is encouraged. \n"
#| "In Europe you would use: Copyright {Year} {Copyright owner}, all rights "
#| "reserved. \n"
#| "In Japan, for maximum protection, the following three items should appear "
#| "in the copyright field of the IPTC Core: (a) the word, Copyright; (b) "
#| "year of the first publication; and (c) name of the author. You may also "
#| "wish to include the phrase \"all rights reserved.\"\n"
#| "This field is limited to 128 ASCII characters.</p>"
msgid ""
"<p>The Copyright Notice should contain any necessary copyright notice for "
"claiming the intellectual property, and should identify the current owner(s) "
"of the copyright for the photograph. Usually, this would be the "
"photographer, but if the image was done by an employee or as work-for-hire, "
"then the agency or company should be listed. Use the form appropriate to "
"your country. USA: &copy; {date of first publication} name of copyright "
"owner, as in \"&copy;2005 John Doe.\" Note, the word \"copyright\" or the "
"abbreviation \"copr\" may be used in place of the &copy; symbol. In some "
"foreign countries only the copyright symbol is recognized and the "
"abbreviation does not work. Furthermore the copyright symbol must be a full "
"circle with a \"c\" inside; using something like (c) where the parentheses "
"form a partial circle is not sufficient. For additional protection "
"worldwide, use of the phrase, \"all rights reserved\" following the notice "
"above is encouraged. \n"
"In Europe you would use: Copyright {Year} {Copyright owner}, all rights "
"reserved. \n"
"In Japan, for maximum protection, the following three items should appear in "
"the copyright field of the IPTC Core: (a) the word, Copyright; (b) year of "
"the first publication; and (c) name of the author. You may also wish to "
"include the phrase \"all rights reserved\".</p><p>With XMP, you can include "
"more than one copyright string using different languages.</p><p>With IPTC, "
"this field is limited to 128 ASCII characters.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>De Kopeerrecht-Angaav schall all nödige Informatschonen bargen, de dat "
"Recht an't intellektuelle Egendom kloorstellt un angeven, wokeen dat "
"opstunns hett. Normalerwies is dat de Fotograaf, man wenn dat en "
"Opdragarbeidt weer oder he för en Bedrief arbeidt, schall de hier stahn. "
"Bruuk de Form, de för Dien Land gellt. USA: &copy; {Johr vun't eerste "
"Apenmaken} Naam vun den Rechtenholler, a.B.: \"&copy; 2005 Klaas Achterndiek"
"\". Ansteed dat \"&copy;\"-Symbool laat sik ok dat Woort \"Copyright\" oder "
"de Afkörten \"copr\" bruken. In en Reeg Länner gellt aver bloots dat Symbool "
"wat. Ok de Formen \"(c)\" un \"(C)\" langt nich. Goot is ok, wenn Du achter "
"de baven angeven Bemarken de Wöör \"all rights reserved\" bruukst.\n"
"In Europa is en propper Form: \"Copyright {Johr} {Rechtenholler}, all rights "
"reserved\".\n"
"In Japan schöölt disse Indrääg binnen dat Copyright-Feld stahn: a) dat Woort "
"\"Copyright\", b) dat Johr vun't eerste Apenmaken, un c) de Naam vun den "
"Maker. Ok hier kannst Du \"all rights reserved\" tofögen.\"\n"
"Dit Feld kann tohööchst 128 ASCII-Tekens bargen.</p>"

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:184
msgid "Right Usage Terms:"
msgstr ""

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:186
msgid ""
"Enter the list of instructions on how a resource can be legally used here."
msgstr ""

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:187
msgid ""
"<p>The Right Usage Terms field should be used to list instructions on how a "
"resource can be legally used.<p>With XMP, you can include more than one "
"right usage terms string using different languages.</p><p>This field does "
"not exist with IPTC.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:195 libs/template/templateviewer.cpp:166
msgid "Source:"
msgstr "Born:"

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:198
msgid "Enter the original owner of the photograph here."
msgstr "Hier kannst Du den Orginaal-Eegner vun dat Bild angeven."

#: libs/template/templatepanel.cpp:200
msgid ""
"<p>The Source field should be used to identify the original owner or "
"copyright holder of the photograph. The value of this field should never be "
"changed after the information is entered following the image's creation. "
"While not yet enforced by the custom panels, you should consider this to be "
"a \"write-once\" field. The source could be an individual, an agency, or a "
"member of an agency. To aid in later searches, it is suggested to separate "
"any slashes \"/\" with a blank space. Use the form \"photographer / agency\" "
"rather than \"photographer/agency.\" Source may also be different from "
"Creator and from the names listed in the Copyright Notice.</p><p>With IPTC, "
"this field is limited to 32 ASCII characters.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Dat Feld \"Born\" warrt för den Orginaaleegner oder den Eegner vun't "
"Copyright bruukt. Na't Opstellen vun't Bild schull nüms dat mehr Feld "
"ännern. Dat warrt noch nich verdwungen, man liekers, bruuk dat Feld bitte as "
"bloots eenmaal schriefbor. As Born schall en Persoon, en Agentur oder en "
"Agenturliddmaat angeven warrn. As Ünnerstütten för later Söökanfragen giff "
"bitte vör un achter Dwarsstreek Freetekens in, also nich \"Fotograaf/Agentur"
"\", man beter \"Fotograaf / Agentur\". De Born kann wat anners wesen as de "
"Maker oder de Naams bi Copyright.</p><p>Dit Feld kann na IPTC tohööchst 32 "
"ASCII-Tekens bargen.</p>"

